we use primarily

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.610
for forecasting a program
and forecasting time

00:12:56.610 --> 00:13:00.330
to market and discount is
called PE Distance, which stands

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.944
for Post-Editing Distance.

00:13:01.944 --> 00:13:03.360
And what you see
here on the chart

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:07.020
is three languages for a
client in the IT domain.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:12.170
And you can see that what you're
going for is the lowest number.

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:15.830
So post-edit distance
means the number

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.910
of changes at a character
level to get from the machine

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.760
translation output
to what you consider

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.310
your human, your gold output.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:28.070
So the idea is, the
less changes you

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:31.340
have to make as a translator,
the more productive you are,

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:32.640
the faster you are.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:35.180
The faster you are, the
faster you can translate,

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:38.780
and therefore the faster the
product can get to market.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:40.430
That's one important thing.

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:44.100
Also, the faster you are and
the more productive you are,

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:46.940
